// Regression (I-13, F-24): a player who is marked out of the GAME but not
// out of the current stage must never be reached by cycle actions
// (`cycle to next` / `cycle to previous`) or the `next`/`previous` player
// expressions. P2 is eliminated mid-stage A; P2 stays in_stage for A/B/C
// (stage entry marks everyone), so every cycle in B and C must skip P2.
player P1, P2, P3
turnorder (P:P1, P:P2, P:P3)
memory WhoNext on table

stage A for current 1 times {
  set P:P2 out of game
  WhoNext is next
  end stage
}

stage B for current 2 times {
  cycle to next
}

stage C for current 2 times {
  cycle to previous
}
